{
  "updated": "2026-10-29",
  "headline": "Built on NVIDIA Nemotron and Nebius: every model call on the live site runs on Nebius Token Factory, the adapter was retrained on Nebius AI Cloud, and the student was served from a Nebius Serverless Endpoint in a measured test.",
  "pitch": "Ratchet is an OpenAI-compatible gateway for license-clean distillation on open models. A small NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Nano 4B student answers first. When it is unsure, the request goes to the teacher, Nemotron 3 Ultra on Nebius Token Factory, and the answer is logged with the teacher's name and license. Night School is built to train a new student from those answers and release it only if it passes a statistical gate. Measured: a Nano adapter taught by Ultra goes from 12.8% to 39.0% on a text-to-SQL exam it never saw, for about $17 on record, and every score recomputes from the saved answers.",
